Formed</th><td class="infobox-data">2001<span style="display: none;"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>(<span class="bday dtstart published updated itvstart">2001</span>)</span><sup about="#mwt10" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-QCAA_brief_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"QCAA brief"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-QCAA_brief-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-QCAA_brief-1" id="mwDA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Jurisdiction</th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Qatar" title="Government of Qatar" class="mw-redirect">Government of Qatar</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><div style="display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0; ">Parent department</div></th><td class="infobox-data">Ministry of Transport and Communication<sup about="#mwt13" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-QCAA_brief_1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"QCAA brief"}}'><a href="#cite_note-QCAA_brief-1" id="mwEA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><div style="display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0; ">Key document</div></th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1126788409" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt15" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Plainlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .plainlist ol,.mw-parser-output .plainlist ul{line-height:inherit;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.mw-parser-output .plainlist ol li,.mw-parser-output .plainlist ul li{margin-bottom:0}</style></span><div class="plainlist"><ul><li style="text-indent: -1em; padding-left: 1em;"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://almeezan.gov.qa/LawPage.aspx?id=3965&amp;language=en" class="external text">Law No. 15 of 2002 on Civil Aviation</a><sup about="#mwt16" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-QCAA_brief_1-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"QCAA brief"}}'><a href="#cite_note-QCAA_brief-1" id="mwFA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFw">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Website</th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="url"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://caa.gov.qa/en-us" class="external text">caa<wbr/>.gov<wbr/>.qa<wbr/>/en-us</a></span></td></tr></tbody></table>

<p id="mwGA">The <b id="mwGQ">Civil Aviation Authority</b> (<b id="mwGg">QCAA</b><!--Qatar Civil Aviation Authority-->, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabic_language" title="Arabic language" about="#mwt18" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"langx","href":"./Template:Langx"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ar"},"2":{"wt":"الهيئة العامة للطيران المدني في قطر"}},"i":0}}]}'>Arabic</a><span about="#mwt18">: </span><span lang="ar" dir="rtl" about="#mwt18">الهيئة العامة للطيران المدني في قطر</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Arabic-language_text" about="#mwt18" id="mwHA"/>) is an agency of the government of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qatar" title="Qatar" id="mwHQ">Qatar</a>. Its head office is in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doha" title="Doha" id="mwHg">Doha</a>.<sup about="#mwt21" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwHw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJg">]</span></span></a></sup> It was established in 2001. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamad_International_Airport" title="Hamad International Airport" id="mwJw">Hamad International Airport</a> in Qatar was developed under the supervision of Civil Aviation Authority (Qatar).</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwKA" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Qatar_Civil_Aviation_Authority&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwKQ">The authority's predecessor, the Civil Aviation Department, was established in 1973.<sup about="#mwt27" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mwKg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLA">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In August 2001, Law No. 16 of 2001 was passed, decreeing the Civil Aviation Department and the Meteorology Department be merged into one entity, thereafter known as the Civil Aviation Authority.<sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

